---
import "../sternzeit/sternzeit.css";
import Term from "../Term.astro";
import "./dunstkreis.css";
---

<figure class="strip-figure wide" id="scattering">
    <div class="strip-panel scattering-panel" data-export="scattering" data-export-timeless>
        <svg aria-hidden="true"></svg>
    </div>
    <figcaption class="figure-caption">
        How strongly the air scatters each wavelength, its <Term of="Scattering coefficient">scattering coefficient</Term>, as
        multiples of red's: by air molecules, <Term of="Rayleigh scattering">Rayleigh scattering</Term>, steeply more towards the violet, and by haze, <Term of="Mie scattering">Mie scattering</Term>, the same at every wavelength. Dashed, the sunlight, and dotted, the skylight it scatters, each
        as a multiple of its own red: the skylight is the sunlight times the air's scattering. Underneath, the two as
        colors, with what each adds up to.
    </figcaption>
</figure>

<script>
    import "./scattering";
</script>
